&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Braze, we have found our people. We’re a genuinely approachable, exceptionally kind, and intensely passionate crew.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to ignite that passion by setting high standards, championing teamwork, and creating work-life harmony as we collectively navigate rapid growth on a global scale while striving for greater equity and opportunity – inside and outside our organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To flourish here, you must be prepared to set a high bar for yourself and those around you. There is always a way to contribute: Acting with autonomy, having accountability and being open to new perspectives are essential to our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our deep curiosity to learn and our eagerness to share diverse passions with others gives us balance and injects a one-of-a-kind vibrancy into our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are driven to solve exhilarating challenges and have a bias toward action in the face of change, you will be empowered to make a real impact here, with a sharp and passionate team at your back. If Braze sounds like a place where you can thrive, we can’t wait to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is an Enterprise-level role within the Enterprise team in Braze&#39;s MEGS (Media, Entertainment, Gaming &amp;amp; Sports) organization. You will own a book spanning NHL, NBA, MLB, and MLS clubs and league-level entities — a mix of existing team/league relationships to grow and protect, combined with a very strong mandate to acquire net-new logos across all four leagues. This is one of the first dedicated, vertical-native seats built for professional sports, with a ~110-day sales cycle that is unique to how teams and leagues plan and budget.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have at least 7+ years selling SaaS solutions into enterprise accounts, with deep comfort running long, multi-stakeholder sales cycles from a standing start. Experience selling into professional sports, media, or live-events organizations is a strong plus, but not required — what matters most is the ability to translate a complex, cross-departmental buying process (marketing, ticketing, digital, data/analytics, and business intelligence functions) into a coherent, value-based pitch, largely from scratch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll operate as the &quot;GM&quot; of your book — building account strategy across a relatively small, high-value universe of teams and league offices, partnering closely with Marketing, Business Development, and Customer Success to build a pipeline that is weighted heavily toward net-new acquisition, while also growing and protecting the existing relationships already in the book.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Core to your pitch will be Braze&#39;s Fan Equity framework: every team and league shares the same lifecycle marketing problem — fan attention peaks hard around game days, season openers, trades, and playoff runs, then falls off in the gaps between. Your job is to show how Braze&#39;s cross-channel orchestration and BrazeAI-powered personalization keep fans engaged through those valleys, turning single-game buyers into season-long, multi-year relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and build pipeline across a named set of NHL, NBA, MLB, and MLS accounts, with a strong emphasis on net-new prospecting and acquisition alongside growth of existing relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute account plans across the book, mapping decision-makers across marketing, ticketing/revenue, digital, and data/analytics functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a consultative, value-based sales process — from discovery through negotiation and close — typically over a ~110-day cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with a Business Development Representative and Marketing to build and prioritize pipeline coverage across the full book&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver executive-level business value assessments that connect Braze&#39;s platform capabilities to team/league-specific outcomes: ticket revenue, sponsorship activation, membership/season-ticket retention, and direct-to-fan digital engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Deal Desk, Strategic Consulting, Customer Success, and Services to structure deals and ensure successful onboarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Braze at relevant industry events, league meetings, and sports-tech forums to build brand presence in the vertical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate forecasting and pipeline hygiene in Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in Enterprise SaaS sales, ideally in Marketing Technology, CDP, CRM, or adjacent categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in complex, multi-stakeholder solution selling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training and practice in value-based selling, with an emphasis on building Business Value Assessments; experience with Command of the Message a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine passion for and working knowledge of the professional sports landscape — how teams and leagues make money, and how fan engagement ties to revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with Salesforce.com CRM or a comparable platform to manage pipeline, required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to quickly ramp on new product surface area and cloud tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record navigating organizations with non-traditional buying committees and decision processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal, written, and executive presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel for in-market meetings and industry events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For candidates based in the United States, the pay range for this position at the start of employment is expected to be between $98,000 and $154,000/year, with an expected On Target Earnings (OTE) between $193,000 and $304,000/year (including bonus or commission). Your exact offer may vary depending on multiple individualized factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. In addition to cash compensation, this role qualifies for a comprehensive Total Rewards package that includes equity grants of restricted stock (RSUs) so that you will own a piece of our company.&lt;/p&gt;
