&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Braze, we have found our people. We’re a genuinely approachable, exceptionally kind, and intensely passionate crew.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to ignite that passion by setting high standards, championing teamwork, and creating work-life harmony as we collectively navigate rapid growth on a global scale while striving for greater equity and opportunity – inside and outside our organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To flourish here, you must be prepared to set a high bar for yourself and those around you. There is always a way to contribute: Acting with autonomy, having accountability and being open to new perspectives are essential to our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our deep curiosity to learn and our eagerness to share diverse passions with others gives us balance and injects a one-of-a-kind vibrancy into our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are driven to solve exhilarating challenges and have a bias toward action in the face of change, you will be empowered to make a real impact here, with a sharp and passionate team at your back. If Braze sounds like a place where you can thrive, we can’t wait to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance team is seeking a Financial Analyst to join our growing Financial Planning &amp;amp; Analysis team. You will be the primary FP&amp;amp;A business partner to the CIO organization, responsible for tracking, forecasting and reporting on key technology metrics and investments across Corporate IT, Business Systems, and Data Analytics functions. You will report to the Manager of FP&amp;amp;A and work closely with CIO leadership and group heads to improve technology financial planning and monthly reporting standards. This role requires someone who is highly analytical and strategic, is able to communicate clearly with both finance and technology leaders, and thrives in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Main responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the CIO organization and business leaders across Corporate IT, Business Systems, and Data Analytics to generate technology operations budgets, forecasts and long-range plans including monthly, quarterly, and annual cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, forecast and report on key technology financial metrics including AI tokenization spend, infrastructure spend, cloud consumption, licensing costs, vendor contracts, and IT operational KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support monthly close process through close partnership with accounting and operations teams, ensuring accurate tracking of technology/AI investments and spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights and commentary on key technology trends, infrastructure investments, cloud migration initiatives, and technology modernization to finance leadership and business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on actual technology financial results against targets, provide variance analysis, assist in guidance on future trends, and present findings to Finance and CIO leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and develop financial models and scenario analyses to support strategic technology decisions, including AI investments, cloud migration, infrastructure investments, and operational efficiency improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge assumptions and provide independent financial perspective on technology strategies, infrastructure investments, and digital transformation initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support LRP and budget planning by translating business requirements and growth targets into technology investment needs and roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad hoc projects and strategic initiatives including contract analysis and cost optimization opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+years of progressive experience in Finance and FP&amp;amp;A, preferably in Tech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergrad degree in Accounting, Finance, Economics, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An analytical, creative thinker who can focus on the details without losing sight of the big picture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling skills and a very high level of comfort with Microsoft Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance multiple responsibilities with competing deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills with the ability to translate complex technology and financial concepts for diverse audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of technology infrastructure, cloud platforms (AWS, Azure), and enterprise technology investments is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial planning and analysis tools such as Pigment or similar platforms is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with business intelligence tools, AI and data analytics platforms is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For candidates based in the United States, the pay range for this position at the start of employment is expected to be between $68,000 and $107,000/year, with an expected On Target Earnings (OTE) between $77,000 and $121,000/year (including bonus or commission). Your exact offer may vary depending on multiple individualized factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. In addition to cash compensation, this role qualifies for a comprehensive Total Rewards package that includes equity grants of restricted stock (RSUs) so that you will own a piece of our company.&lt;/p&gt;
