&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Braze, we have found our people. We’re a genuinely approachable, exceptionally kind, and intensely passionate crew.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to ignite that passion by setting high standards, championing teamwork, and creating work-life harmony as we collectively navigate rapid growth on a global scale while striving for greater equity and opportunity – inside and outside our organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To flourish here, you must be prepared to set a high bar for yourself and those around you. There is always a way to contribute: Acting with autonomy, having accountability and being open to new perspectives are essential to our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our deep curiosity to learn and our eagerness to share diverse passions with others gives us balance and injects a one-of-a-kind vibrancy into our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are driven to solve exhilarating challenges and have a bias toward action in the face of change, you will be empowered to make a real impact here, with a sharp and passionate team at your back. If Braze sounds like a place where you can thrive, we can’t wait to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Braze is the leading customer engagement platform, helping the world&#39;s most ambitious brands build absolutely engaging relationships with their customers. From cross-channel messaging and journey orchestration to AI-powered experimentation and optimization, we put market-leading AI in the hands of marketers in one of the most dynamic categories in software. We&#39;re growing fast and expanding globally, and this role sits right at the center of how we bring that innovation to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our core Product Marketing team defines how the world understands our products. This role is about what happens next: turning that messaging and positioning into a field narrative that wins. You&#39;ll be the connective tissue between Product Marketing and the GTM organization — the person who makes sure everything we bring to market is visible, understandable, and sellable across Sales, Sales Engineering, Customer Success, and Partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a player-coach role. You&#39;ll lead a small, agile team of GTM PMMs while staying hands-on in the work yourself — and you&#39;ll have the runway to grow that team and your scope as Braze scales globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The field narrative:&amp;nbsp;Take the core messaging and positioning built by the PMM team and shape it into a compelling, coherent story the field can carry into every conversation — by persona, segment, and stage of the funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The playbook, and how product information reaches the field:&amp;nbsp;You own the system by which our products become legible to the GTM org: the plays, narratives, assets, and channels that ensure every seller knows what we offer, who it&#39;s for, why it matters now, and how to win against the alternatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technology &amp;amp; services delivery partner GTM:&amp;nbsp;Own how we go to market &lt;em&gt;with&lt;/em&gt; our technology and services delivery partners — enabling them on our products and narrative, partnering strategically on launches and programs, building joint go-to-market motions, and aligning priorities so that our success and our partners&#39; success reinforce each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Braze Services Marketing:&amp;nbsp;Own the GTM narrative for our in-house services — support, onboarding, and education — and articulate the distinct value of Braze-delivered services to our customers as a meaningful differentiator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A small, agile, growing team:&amp;nbsp;Lead and develop a team of GTM PMMs, setting priorities, raising the bar on craft, and building the foundation for a function that will scale globally over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with field leadership every day. Work hand-in-hand with Sales, Solutions Consultants, and CS leaders to understand where deals stall, what reps need, and how to translate product value into language that moves opportunities forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technology into the language of our buyers — and coach the field to do the same: You make hard things simple without making them shallow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI as a force multiplier — judiciously:&amp;nbsp;You&#39;re AI-literate and fluent in how AI is reshaping both martech and the practice of marketing. You know when AI meaningfully accelerates the work and when human judgment has to lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize ruthlessly:&amp;nbsp;Focus your team&#39;s energy on the narratives, launches, and plays that move the needle for the business — and have the judgment and the spine to say no to the rest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend time with customers:&amp;nbsp;You treat customer time as a priority, not a luxury, and you bring what you learn back into the messaging, the playbook, and the roadmap conversation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Success Is Measured&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can measure and report on your work, and you hold yourself accountable to business outcomes — not activity. Success in this role is measured against pipeline, product adoption, pipeline progression, and overall program impact, and you&#39;ll be expected to show that connection clearly and consistently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A marketer who loves working with Sales and Customer Success. You&#39;re energized by the field, not protective of distance from it. The field trusts you as a subject-matter expert; Marketing trusts you as a strategic, thoughtful partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A messaging craftsperson. You can take a positioning doc and a complex product and turn it into something sharp, memorable, and sales-ready. Strong messaging chops are non-negotiable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in the sales motion. You understand how deals actually get done and build for the way the field really sells&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply curious. You ask why. You dig into the product, the market, the competition, and the customer until you understand them well enough to make them simple&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An exceptional writer and presenter. You write with clarity and edge, and you can command a room — a sales kickoff stage, an exec readout, or a field enablement session&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steeped in martech. You bring deep experience in the martech space, including a strong grasp of AI innovations and the competitive landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sharp prioritizer and a builder of trust across cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in Product Marketing, GTM/field marketing, or a closely related GTM function, including experience leading and developing people&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building field-facing narratives and enablement that demonstrably influenced pipeline, deal velocity, or win rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience in B2B SaaS, ideally in martech, with strong command of the competitive and AI landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to translate complex technology into buyer-ready language — and to help a field organization do the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building joint go-to-market motions with technology or services delivery partners — enabling partners, aligning priorities, and partnering on launches and programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate across functions and bring order to ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in marketing as a craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE DETAILS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; VP of Product Marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid; must be based in one of our hub cities — New York (HQ), San Francisco, Chicago, or Austin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to 30%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOW WE WORK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We move fast, we work hard, and we love our jobs. If that sounds like your kind of team, we&#39;d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;For candidates based in the United States, the pay range for this position at the start of employment is expected to be between $166,000 and $245,000/year, with an expected On Target Earnings (OTE) between $191,000 and $273,000/year (including bonus or commission). Your exact offer may vary depending on multiple individualized factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. In addition to cash compensation, this role qualifies for a comprehensive Total Rewards package that includes equity grants of restricted stock (RSUs) so that you will own a piece of our company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Braze benefits vary by location, and we encourage you to review our specific benefits offerings for each country at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.braze.com/company/careers/how-we-hire#benefit-section&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. More details on benefits plans will be provided if you receive an offer of employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From offering comprehensive benefits to fostering hybrid ways of working, we&#39;ve got you covered so you can prioritize work-life harmony. Braze offers benefits such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation that may include equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement and Employee Stock Purchase Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefit plans covering medical, dental, vision, life, and disability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family services that include fertility benefits and equal paid parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development supported by formal career pathing, learning platforms, and a yearly learning stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curated in-office employee experience, designed to foster community, team connections, and innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to give back to your community, including an annual company-wide Volunteer Week and donation matching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups that provide supportive communities within Braze&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, transparent, and fun culture recognized as a Great Place to Work®&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT BRAZE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Braze is the leading customer engagement platform that empowers brands to Be Absolutely Engaging™ Braze helps brands deliver great customer experiences that drive value both for consumers and for their businesses. Built on a foundation of composable intelligence, BrazeAI™ allows marketers to combine and activate AI agents, models, and features at every touchpoint throughout the Braze Customer Engagement Platform for smarter, faster, and more meaningful customer engagement. From cross-channel messaging and journey orchestration to Al-powered decisioning and optimization, Braze enables companies to turn action into interaction through autonomous, 1:1 personalized experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company has repeatedly been recognized as a Leader in marketing technology by industry analysts, and was voted a G2 “Best of Marketing and Digital Advertising Software Product” in 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Braze was also named a 2025 Best Companies To Work For by U.S. News and World Report, a 2025 America’s Greatest Companies by Newsweek, and a 2025 Fortune Best Workplace in Technology™ by Great Place To Work®, among other accolades. Braze is also proudly certified as a Great Place to Work® in the U.S., the UK, Australia, and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in New York with offices in Austin, Berlin, Bucharest, Chicago, Dubai, Jakarta, London, Paris, San Francisco, São Paulo, Singapore, Seoul, Sydney and Tokyo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BRAZE IS AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Braze, we strive to create equitable growth and opportunities inside and outside the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building meaningful connections is at the heart of everything we do, and that includes our recruiting practices. We&#39;re committed to offering all candidates a fair, accessible, and inclusive experience – regardless of age, color, disability, gender identity, marital status, maternity, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. When applying and interviewing with Braze, we want you to feel comfortable showcasing what makes you you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We know that sometimes different circumstances can lead talented people to hesitate to apply for a role unless they meet 100% of the criteria. If this sounds familiar, we encourage you to apply, as we’d love to meet you&lt;/p&gt;
