&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Braze, we have found our people. We’re a genuinely approachable, exceptionally kind, and intensely passionate crew.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to ignite that passion by setting high standards, championing teamwork, and creating work-life harmony as we collectively navigate rapid growth on a global scale while striving for greater equity and opportunity – inside and outside our organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To flourish here, you must be prepared to set a high bar for yourself and those around you. There is always a way to contribute: Acting with autonomy, having accountability and being open to new perspectives are essential to our continued success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our deep curiosity to learn and our eagerness to share diverse passions with others gives us balance and injects a one-of-a-kind vibrancy into our culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are driven to solve exhilarating challenges and have a bias toward action in the face of change, you will be empowered to make a real impact here, with a sharp and passionate team at your back. If Braze sounds like a place where you can thrive, we can’t wait to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE&#39;RE LOOKING FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solutions Operations is the internal capability layer behind Braze&#39;s Solutions Consulting organization. We build the tooling, systems, and telemetry that let the field move faster — so that what works in one region reaches the others while the deal is still live, and no Solutions Consultant rebuilds something that already exists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role exists because the work has changed. Technical Solutions Engineering was built to produce demo assets on request — custom in-app messages, Liquid, web forms, browser scripts. AI-assisted development has compressed most of that, and the field now builds a good deal of it themselves. The opportunity is no longer producing artifacts on request; it&#39;s owning the systems that make the whole organization faster, better informed, and ultimately more effective. This is an operations role with real technical depth: instead of building demo tooling, you&#39;ll build business systems, and you&#39;ll use data from across the global SolCon org to decide what&#39;s worth building at all.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be based in EMEA deliberately. A core part of this role is having a point of view that spans regions — seeing how an AMER enterprise team operates versus an EMEA one, understanding why one pocket of the org wins and another doesn&#39;t, and turning that into something reusable rather than leaving it buried in a single deal or function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an operations, go-to-market engineering, solutions engineering, or technical program management role in B2B SaaS, you&#39;ve owned a system or a program, not just a queue of tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical enough to build: comfortable with scripting and light application development (Python, JavaScript/Node, APIs, SDKs), and fluent with AI development tooling (Claude, Cursor, agent frameworks, MCP). A CS degree is not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-fluent: comfortable in Salesforce, Looker (or similar BI tooling) and a warehouse (Snowflake or similar), able to build your own dashboards and defend the numbers in them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how go-to-market teams actually operate — sales cycles, presales motions, and what makes a technical evaluation succeed or stall&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to build against a set of requirements, and equally able to write the requirements yourself when nobody hands them to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed. Nobody is going to call you into this work; you&#39;ll identify where the leverage is and go there&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator who can hold a room with regional leadership and a working session with engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious about martech, AI tooling, and where technical evaluation is heading as the demo motion gives way to POCs and agent-driven connectivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the shared systems the field deploys into: demo automation, agent and MCP skill packages, workflow plugins, and the discoverable asset repository — built once, centrally, and reused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn field signal into a build backlog: define what we need to know from the SolCon org, instrument how it&#39;s collected, and translate it into prioritized work with a named metric attached&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce insight, not reporting,&amp;nbsp; what happened, why it happened, and what changed as a result. Own a recurring readout to SolCon and sales leadership across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile what different regional teams already measure, and surface the patterns they aren&#39;t looking at, without dictating their metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go find friction qualitatively: talk to SolCons, AEs, and regional leaders about how deals &amp;amp; their own processes actually run, and map how each specialist function supports the deal cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on high-leverage one-off requests where a bespoke build is genuinely the right call — and be the person who can tell the difference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of what the team builds: visible project posts, sprint showcases, and making reusable assets hard to ignore at the moment someone needs them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Field Architecture, POC Program Delivery, Security &amp;amp; Privacy, Tech Partnerships, and RFP Management as the connective layer between them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
