&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote (US) — core hours estimated 9:00 AM–2:00 PM PT Mon–Thu, 9:00 AM–12:00 PM PT Fri &lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt; September 1 – March 30 (~7 months) &lt;strong&gt;Commitment:&lt;/strong&gt; 20–25 hours/week &lt;strong&gt;Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct contract&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our web marketing team runs several parallel workstreams: SEO/AEO, CRO, and quarterly web launches — supported by specialists and cross-functional partners. During a planned leave of absence, execution of each workstream is covered by existing team members. What this role owns is the connective tissue: the meeting rhythm, the follow-ups, and the cross-team communication that keep web marketing coordinated and moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a process-and-communication role managing high velocity workstreams across teams and aligning resourcing and helping leadership make decisions to keep the roadmap on schedule and on scope. You&#39;ll keep the moving pieces together so the team can stay focused on the work itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the operating rhythm.&lt;/strong&gt; Facilitate the weekly SEO/AEO/CRO meeting and keep web team standup mechanics tight: agendas, notes, and action tracking. Attend internal engineering, AEO/SEO, and web meetings and capture the requests and decisions landing on the web team. Sit on agency calls and assist with roadmap and follow ups and action items.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep the roadmap visible.&lt;/strong&gt; Assemble the written web updates broadcast to cross-functional stakeholders (reviewed by the web team lead before distribution) and help prioritize incoming work with input from workstream owners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Groom the backlogs.&lt;/strong&gt; Keep the AEO/SEO and CRO backlogs current: mark items done, capture new requests for triage, and flag when runway is getting thin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track and chase.&lt;/strong&gt; Follow up on action items across workstreams so nothing silently stalls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Escalate with judgment.&lt;/strong&gt; Spot blockers and route them to the right owner: execution questions to the web team lead, program decisions to the program owner. Deliver a weekly one-page status report to leadership so they have visibility without extra meetings. Act as the connective issue across a variety of marketing calls actively identifying which items are related for the web team and will need resourcing or prioritization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support launch coordination.&lt;/strong&gt; Keep the quarterly web launch checklist moving (owners, dates, dependencies) and partner with BizOps on timeline and strategy alignment, including occasional support materials such as slides.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience as a marketing program manager or similar, with exposure to web or digital marketing, ideally in B2B SaaS.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web and demand generation experience a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong meeting facilitator who runs tight, productive sessions and leaves a clear paper trail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communicator, especially in status updates and stakeholder summaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent with backlog and project tracking tools (Asana, Jira, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across functions and driving follow-through without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized, proactive, and reliable, you notice when something is about to stall and act before it does&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report day-to-day to the Sr director of digital with the web experience manager and SEO/CRO managers as your first point of contact for execution questions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For candidates based in the United States, the pay range for this position at the start of employment is expected to be between $30,000-$40,000 over your 6-month tenure. Your exact offer may vary depending on multiple individualized factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&amp;nbsp;(edited)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
